codex
The independent classification is now complete. All five rules are genuine guarded equations of two named summaries; none rewrites a program configuration, none is a separately asserted number-theory fact, none is marked `simplification`, and none was presented as a prior derived theorem. The recurrence matches the frozen loop on adversarial witnesses and detects a flipped-divisor counterfactual. Consequently, the true domain-lemma set is empty, so Stage 4’s empty obligation map and absent target are mathematically appropriate—not merely self-consistent.
Producer provenance, inventory reconstruction, independent classification, and Stage 4 preflight/manifest checks all pass. The launcher mode is classification-only, so the Stage 5 proof audit is correctly inapplicable and its absence has been verified.
  ✓ Record launcher mode, trusted-tool identities, producer hashes, and immutable input hashes
  ✓ Reconstruct the verification-module rule inventory and compare it bijectively with Stage 3
  ✓ Independently classify every local rule from source and operational semantics
  ✓ Rerun Stage 4 preflight and audit manifests, obligations, and fixed target
  ✓ If proof mode, clean-build a fresh copy and audit theorem identity, axioms, and bridges
  → Write complete evidence and self-contained REVIEW.md with the required final pair
